{{!-- About: the publication explaining itself.

Shared by page-about.hbs, custom-about.hbs and the two Layout override templates, so no markup is
duplicated.

The Layout arrives as `layout` — `@custom.page_hero` from the two templates that follow the
setting, a fixed value from the two that pin one (ADR 0006) — and it decides the opener and nothing
else: the figures, the body, the masthead and the subscribe band are the same below either hero.
That is the whole of what the design changes between A1 and A2 here. `{{#post}}` changes the
context, so the argument is read one frame up, as `../layout`; an unrecognised value falls through
to the centred statement.

THE BODY IS THE PAGE'S, AND SO IS THE CLOSING NOTE. The design puts the masthead BETWEEN two
blocks of prose — the mission statement above it and "Get in touch" below — and a Ghost page has
exactly one body. Splitting `{{content}}` is not something a template can do, so the rule this
theme follows elsewhere applies here too: prose the publication wrote is `{{content}}`, data the
theme derives is a section, and the derived sections bracket the prose rather than interrupting
it. The masthead therefore follows the whole body, including the closing note. Recorded as a
Concession in DECISIONS.md.

`mirror-content` is the scoped layer in assets/css/screen.css that restates the design's article
typography for HTML the theme did not write — which is what puts the markers back on the body's
lists and the underline back under its contact link, both of which Preflight strips. --}}
{{#post}}
	{{#match ../layout "Split hero"}}
		{{> "about/hero-split" eyebrow=(t "About")}}
	{{else}}
		{{> "centered-intro" eyebrow=(t "About") headingId="a1-h"}}
	{{/match}}

	{{#match ../layout "Split hero"}}
		{{> "about/stats" padding="pt-14"}}
	{{else}}
		{{> "about/stats"}}
	{{/match}}

	{{#if html}}
		<section
			aria-label="{{t "About this publication"}}"
			class="container pt-18">
			<div class="mirror-content measure mx-auto">{{content}}</div>
		</section>
	{{/if}}

	{{> "about/team"}}

	{{> "newsletter" anchor="about-newsletter" pt="pt-20"}}
{{/post}}
